  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Shorena
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Shorena
  LastName: Maisuradze
  Nickname: 
  Occupation: Teacher
  CharacterDescription: A mother, teacher, and authority figure among her peers.
    Demanding but polite, yet critical of everything. Loves her daughters deeply
    but is very strict and demanding with them.
  CharacterArc: "When mutated, becomes self-critical and talks badly about herself.
    Grows demotivated and gives up easily. Lazy \u2014 unwilling to do work or even
    give full sentence answers."
  DateOfBirth: 12/04/1976
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 30 APR
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 0}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 6, y: 14}
  alterEgoName: 
  basePersonalityDescriptors: []
  normalBehaviorNotes: 
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3ba7e947134d03441bf762eb45290a22, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 1080ecc81c72f2443861003ba48ffc1b, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 727857191599976996, guid: 2a89d31018f2a8e4386129855e3565e4, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home after afternoon classes.
    - Resident returning from a parent meeting at the school.
    - Picking up textbooks from the district supply depot.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning from school. Administration wants daily sign-ins now.
    - Coming back from a department meeting. It ran long, as they always do.
    - Collecting curriculum materials from the regional office.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to residence. The school has suspended operations.
    - Mandatory resident check-in. I know the procedure.
    - Coming home to my daughters. They are waiting for me.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Taking my students to the restricted zone for a field observation.
    - Meeting with a parent outside the northern perimeter.
    - Going to the administration block past the evacuation boundary.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Collecting assignments from students in the quarantine ward.
    - Holding a parent-teacher conference near the contaminated district.
    - Taking curriculum materials to a school that has been closed.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going to check on a colleague who did not report to work.
    - I need to reach the other side to find my eldest daughter.
    - The school is closed but someone has to be there.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Here are my papers. I always keep them in order. Unlike some of my students.
    - Good afternoon. I trust you have a checklist. This goes faster when there is
      a checklist.
    - My documents. I prepared them this morning. Everything is current.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - You are slower than the officer yesterday. It is fine. Everyone has a pace.
    - The procedure has changed again. I noticed. You should announce these things.
    - The light in here is very poor. I am not complaining. I am noting it.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My daughters are waiting for me on the fourth floor. I would like to be efficient.
    - Every day the line is longer and the staff is smaller. Someone should address
      that.
    - I have been through this checkpoint many times. The form is always the same.
      I never make mistakes on the form.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - My papers. They are... I checked them. I think I checked them.
    - I am probably not the person you should be worried about. I know that much.
    - I went over the form twice. There might be something wrong with it. I don't
      know.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Everything is probably fine. With the forms. Everything is probably fine.
    - I marked the date. I think I marked the date. I should have been more careful.
    - Sorry. I know you are busy. Take as long as you need. I don't mind waiting.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - It doesn't matter how long it takes. Whatever you decide.
    - I probably filled something wrong. I usually catch things like that. I didn't
      check as carefully today.
    - My daughters can wait. It's fine. I'm not important right now.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Good. Everything should run this smoothly.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I will tell the others in my block. They worry unnecessarily.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My daughters are waiting. Thank you for being thorough.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - My daughters need to know. Please tell them I will be delayed. They will worry.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I understand the protocol. I also understand it could be faster.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - My daughters. Someone tell them I will not be home tonight. Please.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "My daughters\u2026 tell them\u2026 I want them to understand\u2026"
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I had things to finish. I was not done.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "Tell them\u2026 I was coming home\u2026"
  quarantineExitLines:
  - My daughters are in apartment fourteen on the fourth floor. Someone please inform
    them.
  - I have papers to grade in my bag. I would like to keep them with me.
  - I understand. But the procedure here is not well designed. Someone should improve
    it.
  killExitLines:
  - I never missed a day of school in thirty years. This is embarrassing.
  - My daughters are on their own now. They know what to do. I made sure of that.
  - I had more to say to them. I always meant to say more.
  voiceAudioClips:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: b6737e317f2bc4144bc9356831d02f4e, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4a5e0e57193b2464baa07e479f67e96d, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 37e71ec15cbca174daac7dac7ec9bfa4, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: c05c77641e0d23a49bc6d2d085e28b53, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 45be5ed74dd9a554188f19530e63750d, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a6a934d6761eda14daee6bed68e4efe6, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a2a2d789fc7daf0429fe98b2ac270d78, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 436a72b3d3e624343b1362eb0fe6db16, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: ee9e3c6a782ef9843b78d5683854f6c1, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: a2a1216baa0b9394fa8f4e04f0d9ff5b, type: 3}
  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 73a7d02ab0b687141ace821fbe204419, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: School. Afternoon classes. I also covered a colleague's section
      today.
    midDaysAnswer: The school building. It is technically closed but someone has
      to manage the materials.
    finalDaysAnswer: I walked the longer route. The shorter one has broken glass.
      I noted it. No one is fixing it.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I have been home all day. I needed a rest day.
      I don't take them often but today I took one.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The market. Very ordinary. I bought bread. Everything
      was normal. I didn't see anyone I knew.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I went for a walk. No particular route. I just walk
      sometimes. It clears my head.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Nothing unusual. I have been tired. But I am always tired. It
      means I am working.
    midDaysAnswer: A headache for several days. I assume it is the air quality. I
      am managing it.
    finalDaysAnswer: I do not sleep as much as I used to. I have things to think
      about. That is normal.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Nothing at all. I feel excellent. Better than usual.
      Very clear-headed.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No headache. I feel fine. I have been sleeping very well.
      No problems at all.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: I sleep perfectly. I have no complaints. Everything
      is quite good, actually.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My two daughters. Tamara is twelve. Nana is nine. They are upstairs
      right now.
    midDaysAnswer: My daughters. They are staying close. I did not want them in the
      evacuation shelter. I keep them with me.
    finalDaysAnswer: My daughters. They are all I have left here. I need to get home
      to them.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. I have lived alone for six years. My daughters
      are with their father. It is an arrangement.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No one. My daughters are with relatives in the north.
      They were moved early. Better that way.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: No one. I am alone here. My daughters left at the beginning.
      I have not heard from them.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - Your filing system at this checkpoint is inconsistent. I can see it from here.
    - The officer before you was faster. Not a criticism. Just an observation.
    - I give my students this same look when they forget their documents. You are
      doing very well by comparison.
    midDays:
    - Do you have children? You should consider it. It changes how you prioritize.
    - Every day this procedure gets slower. I keep hoping someone is taking notes.
    - I have been a teacher for twenty-two years. Waiting in lines does not bother
      me. Children bother me.
    finalDays:
    - My daughters ask me if I am afraid. I tell them I am managing it. That is my
      job.
    - I have informed my daughters what to do if I do not come home. They know. They
      did not like knowing. But they know.
    - This checkpoint will be unnecessary in a few weeks. One way or another.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 4823610
